00:08:05.848 --> 00:08:15.232
<v News>戦争の記憶を、どのように若い世代に伝えていくかが、大きな課題になっています。

00:08:15.932 --> 00:08:24.283
<v News>この日、日本の各地では、平和を祈るさまざまな行事が行われました。

00:08:24.983 --> 00:08:29.016
<v Host>Time for a short quiz. Listen and try to answer.

00:08:29.615 --> 00:08:36.120
<v Slow>戦争が終わってから、今年で何年になりますか。

00:08:36.919 --> 00:08:38.696
<v Host>Eighty-one years.

00:08:39.296 --> 00:08:47.072
<v Slow>追悼式に参列した人たちは、何時に黙とうをしましたか。

00:08:47.871 --> 00:08:51.519
<v Host>At noon — they observed one minute of silence.

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:57.711
<v Slow>戦後に生まれた遺族は、何人でしたか。

00:08:58.511 --> 00:09:02.423
<v Host>One thousand eight hundred forty people — the most ever.

00:09:03.024 --> 00:09:17.207
<v Host>That's all for today. August fifteenth is a quiet day of remembrance across Japan, and passing these memories on to younger generations matters more with each passing year. Thank you for listening, and see you tomorrow.

00:09:17.807 --> 00:09:20.207
<v News>また明日。
